<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 03:13:19 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: South Korea prepares for military deployment in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
South Korea is considering sending military assets to the Strait of Hormuz to support freedom of navigation, media reported Thursday, though Seoul denied it had decided on a deployment. Iran launched strikes on American military targets in the Gulf, in retaliation for an attack that killed four people at a wedding on Tuesday night. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44d55ec8-a652-11f1-8684-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VY4ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44d55ec8-a652-11f1-8684-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VY4ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb75ede6-a801-11f1-8538-997226343bce</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 02:56:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44d55ec8-a652-11f1-8684-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VY4ZR.jpg">© Atta Kenare, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith</link><description>
A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03e99b86-a6a7-11f1-a89b-73cec2680c44</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 17:00:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png">© Montage by the Observers </source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Israeli attacks in West Bank at 'unprecedented' level, PNI leader Barghouti says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, the secretary general of the Palestinian National Initiative (PNI) party Mustafa Barghouti said the level of Israeli attacks on Palestinians in the West Bank had become "totally unprecedented". With tensions escalating, activists accuse settlers of operating with total impunity. "Their goal is clear: it is ethnic cleansing," Barghouti stated, calling Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's reaction to the attacks hypocritical.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9a8929c-a6b1-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/BARGHOUTI.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9a8929c-a6b1-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/BARGHOUTI.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cad2f05e-a6b0-11f1-b09a-eb672b3e2093</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 13:26:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Has Iran modified its rocket systems to fire mines into the Strait of Hormuz?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
Fighting escalated in the Middle East over the weekend after US airstrikes on Sunday targeted Iranian rocket launchers on the island of Larak. The exchange of fire was instigated by the US in retaliation against Iran’s new capabilities for firing mines from rockets into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran’s use of rocket launchers to deploy sea mines into the strategic waterway would be unprecedented, but not implausible. Even so, some analysts remain sceptical.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5679bf30-a61a-11f1-87c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fajr-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5679bf30-a61a-11f1-87c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fajr-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e5d00dc-a708-11f1-ae6a-7df714f7ef0c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 05:57:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5679bf30-a61a-11f1-87c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fajr-5.jpg">© Hadi Yazdani, AP</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran hits US targets in Mideast, wedding strikes being probed, Vance says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-hits-us-targets-as-washington-says-probing-wedding-strike</link><description>
Iran said on Thursday it hit US military bases in Kuwait and the UAE in retaliation for a US strike on a wedding party that killed four people and injured nearly 70. While the US military has reiterated that it never targets civilians, Vice President JD Vance said the strike was being investigated.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/decdf7b2-a7c7-11f1-9862-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9ab7109247ff702b409b67379038daf960c895ec.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/decdf7b2-a7c7-11f1-9862-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9ab7109247ff702b409b67379038daf960c895ec.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0081b310-a757-11f1-8a5a-27e4a23fc3aa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 05:19:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/decdf7b2-a7c7-11f1-9862-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9ab7109247ff702b409b67379038daf960c895ec.jpg">© AFP via US Navy handout</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Toppling Iran’s Islamic regime ‘within reach’, Netanyahu says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Thursday voiced confidence that Iran's Islamic republic could soon fall, saying it was weaker than ever as Iran's army said it targeted US bases in the UAE and Kuwait. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/daee442c-7eb9-11f0-8752-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-10T222952Z-768919978-RC2D4GA53WE7-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-NETANYAHU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/daee442c-7eb9-11f0-8752-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-10T222952Z-768919978-RC2D4GA53WE7-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-NETANYAHU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">972e0ef0-a728-11f1-a021-d3eaff42a4f8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 03:08:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/daee442c-7eb9-11f0-8752-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-08-10T222952Z-768919978-RC2D4GA53WE7-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-NETANYAHU.jpg">© Abir Sultan, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran, US trade threats as Tehran blames Washington for wedding strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike</link><description>
Iran and the United States traded threats on Wednesday after their heaviest military exchanges in weeks. Tehran accused Washington of striking a wedding party and called the attack a war crime. President Donald Trump threatened further US strikes, while Iran’s security chief warned Washington would face a “new strategy.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79169d04-a734-11f1-b48b-69393fb41b1c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:22:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png">© 7sobh</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>US-Iran war: Old videos falsely claim to show new attacks on American bases</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1</link><description>
As US-Iran hostilities flare up and strikes resume, so has a wave of misinformation online. Old and unrelated videos are flooding social media, falsely presented as footage of new attacks. As tensions escalate, clips filmed in Dubai, Russia and the US have been misrepresented as Iranian strikes on US bases in the Gulf. Elsewhere, a 68-year-old video of a US nuclear test has been falsely claimed to show Iran detonating mines in the Strait of Hormuz. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746a965a-a70e-11f1-9bb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15220706936a98899a7c8783-61126554.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746a965a-a70e-11f1-9bb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15220706936a98899a7c8783-61126554.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d86616e-a70e-11f1-9462-b37d75498e93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 20:57:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Israeli FM Gideon Sa'ar: 'I hope Iran will not make the mistake of attacking us'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israel's Minister of Foreign Affairs Gideon Sa’ar addressed the resumption in fighting between the US and Iran, and warned that any Iranian attack on Israel would trigger a "severe" response. He also accused Tehran of continuing to pursue "nuclear weapons aspirations", claiming that Israel "will not allow" Iran to achieve them. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03f3b8-a6e8-11f1-aab9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/TAT-SAAR-POUR-MIX.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be03f3b8-a6e8-11f1-aab9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/TAT-SAAR-POUR-MIX.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed61f0d6-a6e0-11f1-b900-bbccc4313f26</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 17:49:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Videos and debris raise questions over alleged US strike on Iranian wedding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding</link><description>
On the evening of September 1, a barrage of US missile and drone attacks on a town in southern Iran allegedly struck a wedding ceremony, killing at least five people, including a four-year-old boy. FRANCE 24 geolocated a direct hit to the civilian building where local residents say the wedding was being held. The building was more than 135 meters from the apparent target, a communications tower.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78860efa-a6ea-11f1-875a-ab9559766e7b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 17:31:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1586076a-a6e5-11f1-9f77-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-09-02-at-5-42-07-PM.png">© Screengrab 7sobh</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel ‘organised and prepared’ to remove Gaza population if US gives green light, Katz says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-israel-organised-and-prepared-to-remove-gaza-population-if-us-gives-green-light-katz</link><description>
Israel is "organised and prepared" to remove Palestininians from Gaza "by every way possible", Defence Minister Israel Katz told reporters Wednesday, adding that there was no alternative "solution" to crisis. The Israeli government was simply waiting for the US to figure out where to take the displaced Gazans, he said.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dba92900-ab4a-11f0-9ad3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25288675368685.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dba92900-ab4a-11f0-9ad3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25288675368685.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a1eebe0-a6db-11f1-b041-c1762cef3722</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dba92900-ab4a-11f0-9ad3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25288675368685.jpg">AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Xi calls on Mideast nations to be ‘masters of their own affairs’ in rare Egypt visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-xi-calls-on-mideast-nations-to-be-masters-of-their-own-affairs-in-rare-egypt-visit</link><description>
Chinese President Xi Jinping on Wednesday called on "the people of the Middle East" to oppose "externalinterference" and consider reshaping the region's security order during a visit to Egypt. The rare visit by the Chinese leader comes as Beijing aims to expand its influence in the region as the Iran war tests the reliability of the traditional US security umbrella in a vital geostrategic zone. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7787cb1e-a6d2-11f1-88a1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244634219317.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7787cb1e-a6d2-11f1-88a1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244634219317.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21d90a86-a6d5-11f1-8697-c3a5f90ffaca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:22:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7787cb1e-a6d2-11f1-88a1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244634219317.jpg">© Khaled Desouki, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>UNIFIL peacekeepers patrol south Lebanon, caught between Israel and Hezbollah</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260902-unifil-peacekeepers-patrol-south-lebanon-caught-between-israel-and-hezbollah</link><description>
Since this spring, about 6 percent of Lebanon has been occupied by the Israeli army. On the ground, around 600 French soldiers from the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) continue to patrol the zone. The delicate peacekeeping mission documents violations of UN resolutions by both Israel and Hezbollah, with its own future highly uncertain. Our France 2 colleagues report, with FRANCE 24's Florent Marchais.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf6e21c2-a6c7-11f1-888f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8849656686a9812fa0edf02-89967507.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf6e21c2-a6c7-11f1-888f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8849656686a9812fa0edf02-89967507.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07c77b54-a61d-11f1-a769-f592bd554b25</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 12:41:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran: US accused of hitting wedding party in latest strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-us-accused-of-hitting-wedding-party-in-latest-strikes</link><description>
#Tehran says at least four people were killed and dozens more wounded in a #US strike on a town near in the south of #Iran, near the Strait of #Hormuz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25c8019a-a6be-11f1-972d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Iran-wedding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25c8019a-a6be-11f1-972d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Iran-wedding.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38fdb1b0-a6be-11f1-952b-d1be7233563a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:11:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says prepared to resume strikes on Iran at 'any time'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping</link><description>
President Donald Trump on Wednesday suggested he was ready to strike Iran again “at any time" after he proposed renaming the Strait of Hormuz the “Trump Strait.” Earlier, Iran had attacked US military bases in the Gulf following another round of US airstrikes on Iranian soil. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ba7fce-a094-11f1-8493-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236684484728.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ba7fce-a094-11f1-8493-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236684484728.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">118f5bdc-a66f-11f1-afdc-1bc7a8b22ec1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:38:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ba7fce-a094-11f1-8493-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236684484728.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US and Iran trade fire as hostilities flare again</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-us-and-iran-trade-fire-as-hostilities-flare-again</link><description>
The US military hit targets in Iran on Tuesday as Tehran reponded with retaliatory strikes as hostilities between the two countries flared once again in an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. One US strike hit a home hosting a wedding, killing four people and wounding dozens, local officials said. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53de1b6-a63f-11f1-a17a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VZ6NN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53de1b6-a63f-11f1-a17a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VZ6NN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">137d0716-a631-11f1-869d-af91c05e98b9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:15:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53de1b6-a63f-11f1-a17a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6VZ6NN.jpg">© Atta Kenare, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>A Hezbollah hideout stuffed with cash? Nope, this video was AI-generated</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-hezbollah-hideout-stuffed-cash-ai-generated</link><description>
A number of pro-Israel social media accounts have shared a video they claim shows wads of cash and stacks of gold bars in a cache belonging to a deceased Hezbollah leader. There's only one issue: the footage was created using AI. The original video was shared by an Egyptian satirical site.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c754a294-a5dc-11f1-885a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Mode%CC%80le-1920-x-1080-14.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c754a294-a5dc-11f1-885a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Mode%CC%80le-1920-x-1080-14.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62faca4c-a5cf-11f1-a499-d765139e7fa3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 10:01:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c754a294-a5dc-11f1-885a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Mode%CC%80le-1920-x-1080-14.png">© Montage by the FRANCE 24 Observers</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu's wife shares conspiracy claim that opposition leader knew of Oct 7 attacks in advance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-netanyahu-s-wife-shares-conspiracy-that-opposition-leader-had-early-knowledge-of-oct-7-attacks</link><description>
As Israel prepares for what are expected to be close-fought parliamentary elections in October, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's wife Sara on Monday shared a conspiracy theory that centre-left opposition figure Yair Golan had advance warning of the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6639a6e-a5e2-11f1-ad39-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26111417795307.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6639a6e-a5e2-11f1-ad39-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26111417795307.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e9d5e04-a5e2-11f1-a838-4312efd22778</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:36:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6639a6e-a5e2-11f1-ad39-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26111417795307.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US military striking targets in Iran after attempted attacks on shipping</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again</link><description>
The US military said on Tuesday it is striking new targets in Iran as hostilities flare again after a month without military action. US Central Command said that the strikes follow recent attempted attacks by the Iranian government against commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8c81e48-a591-11f1-9a26-2d6b79c37be8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 03:38:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump threatens to ‘hit Iran hard’ as strikes resume after month-long lull</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull</link><description>
President Donald Trump said Monday that the US would hit back against Iranian attacks on US targets in the Middle East, according to a Fox News reporter. The Iranian attacks were themselves a response to US strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first flare-up in a month.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6a05eba-a57a-11f1-a76a-fb7aabece8fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:36:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg">© via Reuters/Wana News Agency</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump vows to hit back 'hard' after first exchange of fire with Iran in weeks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks</link><description>
Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran "hard" after the two foes traded fire for the first time in over a month, while Iran's president warned that more fighting with the US was not in his country's interest. After six months of war, the foes remain at an impasse, with Iran keeping the strategic Strait of Hormuz closed and the US persisting with a naval counter-blockade of Iran. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61eaaa56-8a5d-11f1-8f74-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C39X7A2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61eaaa56-8a5d-11f1-8f74-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C39X7A2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d277974-a56a-11f1-9374-435f773a4b38</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:37:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Raising the Altalena: Netanyahu digs up sunken 1948 arms ship in ‘pre-election stunt’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt</link><description>
A ship carrying arms for a right-wing militia, the Altalena was sunk 78 years ago off the coast of Tel Aviv at the orders of Israel’s founders. The discovery of its wreckage last week has given the country’s right-wing government ammunition to target the left and attempt to redirect the campaign for legislative elections in October.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03fb2ff4-a54e-11f1-ba53-494925e89fd0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:54:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg">© Wikimedia Creative Commons</source><dc:creator>Stéphanie TROUILLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Latest flare-up between US and Iran bring conflict's lull to an end</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end</link><description>
Iran's foreign minister has accused Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu of tricking the United States into war with the Islamic Republic. Over six months into the conflict, there appears to be no end in sight. This after the US struck sites in Iran, prompting Tehran to respond. An April ceasefire brought an end to intense fighting, but sporadic attacks have continued over the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran's closure of the waterway during the conflict has pressured global oil markets, and in turn Donald Trump at home.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8f0074e-a54f-11f1-a0e9-9fe11a5e0a83</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:33:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Strait of Hormuz accessibility at the centre of US-Iran war flare-up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up</link><description>
For the first time in a month, the US has launched strikes against Iran. The attack targeted the shipping island of Larak in the Strait of Hormuz. The US says it was aimed at preventing Tehran from placing sea mines in the strategic shipping lane, just days after Washington announced it had completed clearing explosives from there. Iran then reiterated its attacks, saying it had struck two US military bases in Jordan. FRANCE 24's Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahi tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11e4d97c-a539-11f1-b130-bb4a68c160c1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:47:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Relentless heat worsens Gaza's ongoing struggle to access water</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water</link><description>
In Gaza, securing drinking water is a relentless daily struggle. The war with Israel has destroyed critical water and sanitation infrastructure, and as temperatures soar, the extreme heat is escalating an already severe shortage into a deadly humanitarian crisis. Two and a half years of war with Israel have damaged or destroyed nearly 90% of Gaza’s water and sanitation infrastructure according to UNICEF.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/240c99ec-a529-11f1-8aad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9629343336a955b618609c3-22073425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/240c99ec-a529-11f1-8aad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9629343336a955b618609c3-22073425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4d89c98-a525-11f1-8e66-9904c0de4c4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:49:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran, US trade fire in first exchange in a month</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-iran-us-trade-fire-in-first-exchange-in-a-month</link><description>
Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East on Monday in retaliation following American strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first exchange of fire for a month in a war that has engulfed the region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fa00686-a528-11f1-a2b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-29.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fa00686-a528-11f1-a2b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-29.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b0093ec-a528-11f1-944f-9dca7ebcfc2a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:49:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East war flares up after Iran responds to US attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-war-flares-up-after-iran-responds-to-us-attacks</link><description>
Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East in retaliation for the first American strikes on its territory in a month. This signs a fresh flare-up of the war that has engulfed the region. Washington said its attacks were aimed at preventing Iran from placing more sea mines in the strait and as it threatens new secondary economic sanctions. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah is in Tehran and tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a984b044-a224-11f1-800d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213442630871.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a984b044-a224-11f1-800d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213442630871.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369070de-a524-11f1-9e55-9904c0de4c4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:43:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US renews attack on Iran while threatening financial sanctions on Tehran allies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-renews-attack-on-iran-while-threatening-financial-sanctions-on-tehran-allies</link><description>
Hostilities between the US and Iran resumed after a month's pause. The US said Iran was preparing to launch sea mines into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran retaliated by hitting US military bases in Jordan. Meanwhile, the US Treasury Secretary said there would be more economic sanctions on the way for banks doing business with Iran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be5cd37e-a51d-11f1-b08c-41b48f6f83b3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:40:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran says continuing war ‘not in our interest’ after fighting flares</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian said Monday that continuing the war with the United States was not in his country's interest, following a fresh military flare-up between the two countries after a month-long lull. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6f7a1b4-a4c5-11f1-8a83-31d4a2f58c7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:02:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1532ba2-a4af-11f1-adf9-71be596dc8a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:27:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg">© Atta Kenare, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
